  "usage_note": "**Sit down** is the movement into a seat; **sit** or **be sitting** is the position: *She sat down* (she moved) and *She was sitting by the window* (she was there). *Please sit down* is the usual polite way to offer someone a seat; *Please have a seat* or *Please take a seat* is more formal.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "I sat down the chair.",
      "correct": "I sat down on the chair.",
      "note": "Put **on**, **in**, or **at** before the seat or the table."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "He was sitting down by the window all afternoon.",
      "correct": "He was sitting by the window all afternoon.",
      "note": "For a long time in one position, **sit** alone is more natural."
    }
  ],
